+**Automatic install.** With `[updates] auto_install = true` (the default) a pending update
+installs by itself as soon as no session is running. Each version is tried once: if that install
+fails, the app doesn't retry it, and you can still click **Install & restart**. Set
+`auto_install = false` to install only when you click.
+
+**GitHub Releases.** When `main` has a `VERSION` with no release yet, the Release workflow
+(`.github/workflows/release.yml`) builds the macOS app (zip and `.dmg`) and the Windows
+installer and publishes them as GitHub Release `v<version>`. Those builds are on the `github`
+update channel: every `[updates] github_interval_s` seconds (default 3600, and on **Check now**) they look
+at the repo's latest release. When it is newer, they download the asset for their platform into
+the updates folder, and the folder updater above takes it from there. Builds you make locally
+(`make app`, `make release`) are on the `local` channel and never call GitHub.
+
+On Windows a release is the installer. To install it, a PowerShell helper stops the app, runs
+the installer silently (`/S`) and starts the app again. Rollback isn't available there.
+
 **First install.** An app built before this feature can't update itself. Install once by
 hand, then updates arrive in-app:
 
